  "notes": "{統合|とうごう} means combining separate elements into a unified whole. Used broadly across business, IT, politics, and organizational contexts.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {他動詞|たどうし} (transitive)\n- Takes を: システムを{統合|とうごう}する\n- Passive common: {統合|とうごう}される (to be integrated/merged)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {経営|けいえい}{統合|とうごう}: business integration, merger\n- システム{統合|とうごう}: system integration\n- {統合|とうごう}{失調症|しっちょうしょう}: schizophrenia (medical term)\n- {地域|ちいき}{統合|とうごう}: regional integration\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {合併|がっぺい}: merger (specifically of companies or municipalities)\n- {連携|れんけい}: cooperation, coordination (looser than {統合|とうごう})\n- {一元化|いちげんか}: centralization (bringing under one authority)\n- {統一|とういつ}: unification (often political or standardization)",
